9
00:59:37,500 --> 00:59:43,500
Dinner in America is a 2020 American coming-of-age dark comedy film
written, directed, and edited by Adam Carter Rehmeier.

10
01:06:15,000 --> 01:06:21,000
It stars Kyle Gallner, Emily Skeggs, Griffin Gluck, Pat Healy, Mary Lynn
Rajskub, David Yow, Hannah Marks, Nick Chinlund, and Lea Thompson.

11
01:12:52,500 --> 01:12:58,500
The plot follows a punk rock singer (Gallner) on the run and a young woman
(Skeggs) obsessed with his band who unexpectedly cross paths.

12
01:19:30,000 --> 01:19:36,000
The film premiered at the Sundance Film Festival on January 24, 2020, earning
critical acclaim for its energy and the performances of the leads.

13
01:26:07,500 --> 01:26:13,500
After struggling to find distribution, it was
self-released in the United States on May 27, 2022.

14
01:32:45,000 --> 01:32:51,000
In 2024, the film developed a cult following after being rediscovered and
gaining popularity on TikTok, leading to a second theatrical run.

15
01:39:22,500 --> 01:39:28,500
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
